  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Ki sphere collection determines attack type—collecting 12+ Ki orbs triggers the character's Super ATK (strongest attack). Position your highest-damage character to collect the most Ki orbs by planning the collection order.",
      "Link Skills activate when two characters in the same slot have matching links—team building prioritises characters with overlapping Link Skills (e.g., Saiyan or Super Saiyan) to stack passive bonuses.",
      "Leader Skills require specific character types—build teams where 100% of characters match both Leader Skills (your Leader + Friend Leader) to receive the maximum dual-Leader multiplier.",
      "Dokkan Awakening raises a character's maximum level and abilities—the highest-priority Awakening is any character at \"hidden potential\" Level 10 that gains a new Super ATK or Passive after awakening.",
      "The Hidden Potential system unlocks passive stat nodes at 55%/69%/79%/100% unlock milestones—prioritise the 55% milestone (provides the first passive stat boost) before the 100% completion for cost efficiency."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "Ki球の収集が攻撃タイプを決定する。12以上のKiを収集するとキャラクターの超必殺技（最強の攻撃）が発動する。収集順序を計画して最も高いダメージのキャラクターが最も多くのKi球を収集できる位置に配置する。",
      "リンクスキルは同じスロットの2人のキャラクターが一致するリンクを持つ時に発動する。チーム構成はパッシブボーナスを積み重ねるためにリンクスキルが重複するキャラクター（例：サイヤ人または超サイヤ人）を優先する。",
      "リーダースキルは特定のキャラクタータイプを必要とする。最大のデュアルリーダー乗数を受け取るために、100%のキャラクターが両方のリーダースキル（自分のリーダー+フレンドリーダー）に一致するチームを構築する。",
      "ドッカン覚醒はキャラクターの最大レベルと能力を引き上げる。最優先の覚醒は、覚醒後に新しい超必殺技やパッシブを得る「限界突破」レベル10のキャラクター。",
      "潜在能力システムは55%/69%/79%/100%のアンロックマイルストーンでパッシブステータスノードを解放する。コスト効率のために100%完成より先に55%マイルストーン（最初のパッシブステータスブーストを提供する）を優先する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Starting Team Building",
        "body": "Build your first team from the initial tutorial summons around a rainbow leader (a Leader Skill that works for all types) or a type-specific leader if you pulled a 5+ star character with a strong Type Leader Skill. The most accessible strong starter teams use the \"All Type\" or \"TEQ\" category leaders that accept any character—these leaders provide lower per-character multipliers but allow including the highest-ATK characters from your initial pull roster without type restrictions."
      },
      {
        "title": "Dragon Stone Management",
        "body": "Dragon Stones (premium currency) are available from events, story completion, and daily missions. Save stones exclusively for Dokkan Fest banners (highest rate for top-tier characters) and Step-Up banners (discounted first step, higher rates on steps 3+). Never use Dragon Stones on normal banners unless you have 200+ stones and no upcoming Dokkan Fest within 2 weeks. Stone income from main story completion is approximately 1000+ stones for first-time clears."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Extreme Z-Battle Farming",
        "body": "Extreme Z-Battle provides a method to strengthen base-card characters beyond Dokkan Awakening—feeding medals from Extreme Z-Battle stages activates bonus passive effects on older characters. The critical decision: only invest Extreme Z medals in characters that remain relevant in the current meta. Check tier lists before spending medals on older characters whose passive effects no longer match modern fight requirements. Priority targets: characters with unique niche roles (INT type with barrier break, PHY type with multi-hit EZA passive)."
      },
      {
        "title": "Event Farming Priority",
        "body": "Dokkan Events provide awakening medals for transforming 4-5 star characters into their Dokkan Awakened forms—farm event medals immediately on release as event difficulty and bonus multipliers reset periodically. The 30-stamina event stage (highest difficulty per event) provides 3× the medals per stamina of lower stages. Complete event stages on the highest available difficulty to maximise medal efficiency during limited event windows."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Team Optimization for Endgame Quests",
        "body": "Multi-Stage Super Battle Road and Infinite Dragon Ball History events require complete type-diverse teams since each stage can have different type counters. Build teams with at least 2 characters from each of the 5 types (STR, AGL, TEQ, INT, PHY) in your total available roster, then selectively deploy the appropriate type combination per stage. End-game events typically require 4–6 duplicates of the same character to unlock Full Power hidden potential nodes for maximum damage output."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Using Dragon Stones to revive in battle—revival stones restore HP but provide no progression value; save all stones for summons since the investment ROI of a revival is near zero.",
      "Building teams with mixed types when a type-specific team is available—type-matching Leader Skills in Dokkan provide 2.5–3.5× the multiplier of mixed-type alternatives; always prefer type purity when the roster supports it.",
      "Ignoring passive skills when selecting characters—characters with triggering passives (transform at 50% HP, activate super at turn 2) require specific team configurations to trigger; passive conditions must be consistently achievable in your typical battle flow.",
      "Not completing the daily missions—daily missions provide guaranteed Dragon Stones and training items; missing them consistently over two weeks costs the equivalent of 3–4 multi-summon pulls.",
      "Awakening characters before checking if a Super Awakening is available—Super Awakening is a more powerful upgrade path than standard Dokkan Awakening for certain characters; attempt Super Awakening first if the character has that path available."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "戦闘でドラゴンストーンを蘇生に使う。蘇生ストーンはHPを回復するが進行価値はない。蘇生のROIはほぼゼロなので、全てのストーンを召喚のために貯める。",
      "タイプ固有のチームが利用可能な時に混合タイプのチームを構築する。ドッカンのタイプマッチングリーダースキルは混合タイプの代替の2.5〜3.5倍の乗数を提供する。ロースターがサポートする場合は常にタイプ純度を優先する。",
      "キャラクターを選択する時にパッシブスキルを無視する。トリガーパッシブを持つキャラクター（HP50%で変身、2ターン目に超発動等）は特定のチーム構成をトリガーするために必要。パッシブ条件は典型的な戦闘フローで一貫して達成可能でなければならない。",
      "デイリーミッションを完了しない。デイリーミッションは保証されたドラゴンストーンとトレーニングアイテムを提供する。2週間にわたって一貫して見逃すと、3〜4回のマルチ召喚引き相当を失う。",
      "スーパー覚醒が利用可能かどうかを確認する前にキャラクターを覚醒させる。スーパー覚醒は特定のキャラクターの標準ドッカン覚醒より強力なアップグレードパス。キャラクターがそのパスを利用できる場合は先にスーパー覚醒を試みる。"
